  "body": "When the options to choose are many, instead of using &lt;select&gt;, an input and a &lt;datalist&gt; dynamically filled with a search in a data source can be used. Javascript is used to do this, but it is something so basic that the browser could do it without the need for Javascript, it would only be necessary to indicate the source of the data.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<input list=\"article-list\" name=\"article\" type=\"text\" />\r\n<datalist id=\"article-list\" src=\"/article?lang=en&view=json\" />\r\n\r\nExample query URL with a search parameter added with the content of the input: \"/article?lang=en&view=json&search=Ne\"\r\n```",
